      <!-- Search -->
      <meta name="description" its:translate="yes">Use an FQDN as a unique and absolute digital address to ensure Internet traffic, e-mails and security certificates reach a specific server without any risk of ambiguity or misdirection.</meta>
      <abstract>
        <variablelist>
          <para>A Fully Qualified Domain Name (FQDN) is an absolute network identifier specifying a host's exact position within the Domain Name System hierarchy in &productname;. By combining a host name with its complete domain path, an FQDN ensures unambiguous network addressing across global networks, enables SSL/TLS security certificate validation, and guarantees reliable mail delivery without misdirection.</para>
